    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **James Wood** leading the charge, posting a stellar 78.28 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Burrows (xERA 4.71) and prime leadoff placement create an ideal environment for him to catalyze our run production. Following closely is **Corbin Carroll**, who benefits from the elite speed mandate of our strategy; he remains a high-floor start against Buehler, with his dynamic platoon advantage and top-tier order placement cementing his 73.03 score. **Isaac Paredes** also rounds out our high-leverage tier at 72.13, capitalizing on a significant skill gap against Mikolas, where his 14% SP skill advantage and position in the three-hole provide a clear path to driving in runs.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational tightropes, most notably the 60.04 score for **Austin Riley**, whose utility start is marred by a 34% rain risk and a difficult encounter with Peralta. While he makes the cut, the decision to bench other depth pieces was guided strictly by the efficiency scale; **Dalton Rushing** and **Jose Caballero** both sit near the 40\u201342 range\u2014well below our preferred threshold\u2014but remain in the lineup due to the lack of viable replacements. **Kyle Karros** was a pleasant surprise today, jumping to 63.93 thanks to a massive 19% SP skill edge against Lauer. The most difficult bench decision was opting against rolling with our available reserves, as the optimizer held firm on excluding **Mickey Moniak** and others due to lineup inactivity, prioritizing the limited game caps for the active group of **Brice Turang**, **Gabriel Moreno**, and company. We remain vigilant on **Austin Riley**\u2019s weather status as we look to capitalize on the SB-heavy profile of our core.",
